    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Exceptional period artisan 780 sq.ft. property that was fully renovated with a double storey extension. Located off Sarsfield road classified by Google maps as Kilmainham. Eircode D10X446. Rated as a safe area by Deliveroo couriers (map attached) and was the original Inchicore that housed the CIE and Guinness workers. Well connected to the City Centre (3 miles city centre) and James st. hospital. Well insulated property with low running costs BER C Energy rated.  2 bedrooms (1 double and 1 single bedroom) with 2 ensuites (one with a bath !) and a downstairs WC. Soundbloc boards installed. Designer kitchen with built-in whirlpool appliances. Wireless sound system with recessed ceiling speakers. Solid oak flooring and antique open fireplace in the lounge. Private bedrooms (new 5ft bed and a 4 ft small double) with semi-solid natural ash floors. Porcelain tiled bathrooms with silent thermostatic power showers. Venetian blinds throughout including 6 velux windows giving great natural light. HKC Certified alarm system with mobile phone control and event updates. Floored attic space via pull down Stirra. Loft aerial with a Sky satellite disk. Each room has an intercom and wired with Co-ax and ethernet. Partially enclosed courtyard with secure rear pedestrian access with key. Beside Longmeadows Pitch and Putt, Liffey Gaels park (see Street view) with pedestrian overhead bridge to the Memorial Gardens. Street where Thomas Kinsella grew up having a happy childhood. Web search Thomas Kinsella The Ranch for a podcast of this blue collar area. Free on-street parking (no permits required). Standard references required. Affordability index set at 35%"
      }
